# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Expense vs Sales — Phase A/B artefacts, held local at Ahmed's instruction
# (2026-08-09) until the data foundation is signed off.
#
# expense/ carries the reviewable mapping table and the reconciliation reports.
# expense_sku_map.csv holds human sign-off decisions, so when this is lifted the
# folder must be committed, not regenerated -- a rebuild without it would
# discard every ratified mapping.
#
# NOTE FOR WHOEVER LIFTS THIS: cache/ is blanket-ignored above, so
# cache/expense_budget.data.js will NOT be pushed by a normal commit. The
# existing caches are only in the repo because they were tracked before that
# rule was added. Going live needs an explicit  git add -f cache/expense_budget.data.js
# or the deployed page will request a script that is not there.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
expense/
etl/build_expense_foundation.py
etl/apply_expense_decisions.py
etl/build_expense_cache.py
etl/verify_expense_page.js
etl/verify_expense_render.js

# Node dev dependencies. The platform ships no npm packages -- these exist only
# because the Expense verification harness uses jsdom to render the page in a
# real DOM outside a browser. Ignored so a stray `npm install` can never sweep
# ~1,800 library files into a commit.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

